<h2>Segment 322 &mdash; twelve instants ending black deeds</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s322S">[iv.241-8] ,<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w1"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w2">zad</span> par <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w3">byed</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w4">tshul</span> ni, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w5"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w6">chos</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w7">bzod pa</span></span> zhi <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s322w8">dang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w9">&#x27;dod chags</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w10">bral ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w11"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w12">bar chad med</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w13">lam</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w14">brgyad</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w15">sems pa</span> gang yin pa <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w16">rnam pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w17">bcu gnyis</span> po <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w18">de</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w19">nag po</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w20">zad</span> par <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w21">byed</span> pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w22">las</span> yin te, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w23">&#x27;dod</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w24">nyon</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w25">spong</span> bar <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w26">byed</span> pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s322w27">phyir</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s322S">Here is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w4">how</span> these deeds are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w1"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w3">brought</span> to an <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w2">end</span></span>. First let&#x27;s take the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w17">twelve</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w16">types</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w15">mental movement</span> had with the four instants known as &quot;the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w5"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w7">mastery</span> of <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w6">phenomena</span></span>,&quot; <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s322w8">as well as</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w14">eight</span> instants of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w11"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w12">uninterrupted</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s322w13">path</span></span> [part of the path of seeing, the direct perception of selflessness] which is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w10">free of</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w9">desire</span>. <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w18">These</span> are the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w22">deeds</span> that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w21">act</span> to bring <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w19">black</span> deeds to an <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w20">end</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s322w27">for</span> they <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w26">function</span> to <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w25">eliminate</span> all the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w24">mental afflictions</span> that relate to the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s322w23">desire realm</span>.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, independent reconciliation. ZHI/zhi is not aligned with four; the probable numeral-spelling question remains an editorial query, and no source correction is applied. The second ending causative is discontinuous, so zad/end and byed/act retain only the tighter lexical atoms. The introductory causative keeps its unique end and brought members. Repeated deeds, desire and causatives select their stated source occurrences. Supplied participants, brackets and distributed grammar remain unwrapped; omission is not a null. No hgm_gloss promotion.</div>
